---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Tenure Preview | AI Proxy for memory and agent enforcement"
  description="Request free access to the Tenure preview. Observe agent behavior, draft policy, enforce capabilities and preconditions, and inspect every runtime decision."
  canonical="https://tenureai.dev/preview"
  keywords="Tenure preview, AI agent governance preview, agent policy enforcement, AI runtime enforcement, agent observability, self-hosted AI governance"
>
  <main class="preview-page">
    <section class="preview-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">Tenure Public Preview</span>
        <h1>The model does the thinking.<br /><span>Tenure does the policing.</span></h1>
        <p class="preview-lede">
          Give every AI request the right institutional memory, then apply deterministic policy before an agent action reaches your systems. The Tenure Pro Preview is free and self-hosted, with no per-agent, per-client, or per-project limits.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row">
          <a href="mailto:contact@tenureai.dev?subject=Tenure%20Pro%20Early%20Access" class="btn-primary">Request Preview Access</a>
          <a href="/how-it-works" class="btn-secondary">See How It Works</a>
        </div>
        <p class="access-note">Request access by email today. We will send access details when the preview is ready on Friday, August 14th.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="preview-section section-surface">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">What is included</span>
        <h2>Governed memory and agent enforcement, free for individual use.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          Tenure gives the model scoped context and governs what the agent can do with it. Memory and enforcement run together on the same authenticated request path.
        </p>

        <div class="preview-pillars">
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Memory</span>
            <h3>What should the model know?</h3>
            <p>Inject only active, relevant institutional knowledge from scopes the caller is allowed to access.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Policy</span>
            <h3>What may the agent do?</h3>
            <p>Expose only reviewed capabilities, then check every returned action before it reaches your runtime.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Preconditions</span>
            <h3>What must be true first?</h3>
            <p>Require evidence from earlier steps before a dependent action can continue.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="request-flow" aria-label="Tenure preview workflow">
          <article class="flow-card">
            <span>01</span>
            <strong>Observe</strong>
            <small>Record the tools an agent sees, the calls it makes, and the results passed between steps.</small>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
          <article class="flow-card">
            <span>02</span>
            <strong>Draft</strong>
            <small>Turn observed behavior into a capability policy your team can inspect.</small>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
          <article class="flow-card">
            <span>03</span>
            <strong>Review</strong>
            <small>Choose the allowed tools, arguments, and required preconditions.</small>
          </article>
          <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
          <article class="flow-card featured-flow">
            <span>04</span>
            <strong>Enforce</strong>
            <small>Hide forbidden tools and withhold unauthorized actions before execution.</small>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="included-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Agent governance</span>
            <h3>Observe and enforce</h3>
            <p>Agent observability, automatic policy drafts, policy enforcement, and reviewed preconditions are included.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Governed memory</span>
            <h3>Carry institutional knowledge across AI tools</h3>
            <p>Project-scoped memory, structured beliefs with provenance, scoped tokens, persona controls, and injection logs are included.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="card-label">Operations</span>
            <h3>Keep the record</h3>
            <p>Full audit history and exports, backup and restore tooling, local deployment, and community support are included.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="preview-section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="label">Preview versus paid tiers</span>
        <h2>Use the product now. Add organizational controls later.</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">
          The preview gives a single operator the Community memory foundation and Pro agent-governance workflow for free. Features for sharing memory, identity, policy, and administration across teams and organizations remain gated to paid tiers when those plans launch.
        </p>

        <div class="tier-grid">
          <article class="tier-card preview-tier">
            <div class="tier-kicker">Free preview</div>
            <h3>Included now</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Project-scoped memory</li>
              <li>Structured beliefs with provenance</li>
              <li>Scoped client and agent tokens</li>
              <li>Persona controls and injection logs</li>
              <li>Agent observability</li>
              <li>Automatic policy drafts</li>
              <li>Agent policy enforcement</li>
              <li>Capabilities and preconditions</li>
              <li>Full audit history and exports</li>
              <li>Backup and restore tooling</li>
              <li>Unlimited projects, clients, and agent tokens</li>
              <li>Self-hosted deployment</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="tier-card">
            <div class="tier-kicker">Paid Team later</div>
            <h3>Multi-user operation</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Team Mode</li>
              <li>OAuth and OIDC</li>
              <li>Separate user identities and access</li>
              <li>Project and team scopes</li>
              <li>Shared team context</li>
              <li>Centralized team audit history</li>
              <li>Ticket support</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="tier-card">
            <div class="tier-kicker">Paid Enterprise later</div>
            <h3>Organization-wide control</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>SAML SSO</li>
              <li>SCIM provisioning and deprovisioning</li>
              <li>Group-to-scope mapping</li>
              <li>Organization-wide policy controls</li>
              <li>Audit retention controls</li>
              <li>Private deployment options</li>
              <li>Faster support</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="boundary-note">
          <strong>The boundary is simple.</strong> The free preview gives one operator governed memory and agent enforcement. Paid tiers add shared team memory, multi-user identity, centralized administration, and organization-wide controls when multiple people and teams operate Tenure together.
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="preview-section section-surface">
      <div class="container access-container">
        <span class="label">Access</span>
        <h2>Ready Friday, August 14th.</h2>
        <p>
          Preview access is free. Use the request button to email us now, and we will send the access details when the preview opens. Tenure remains self-hosted, so your memory, policies, audit trail, and agent activity stay in your environment.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-row">
          <a href="mailto:contact@tenureai.dev?subject=Tenure%20Pro%20Early%20Access" class="btn-primary">Request Preview Access</a>
          <a href="/pricing" class="btn-secondary">Compare Plans</a>
        </div>
        <p class="cta-meta">Free preview <span>·</span> Self-hosted <span>·</span> No call-home telemetry</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .preview-page *,
    .preview-page *::before,
    .preview-page *::after {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    .preview-hero {
      padding: 7rem 2rem 5rem;
      text-align: center;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 50% 15%, rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.1), transparent 35%),
        var(--bg);
    }

    .preview-hero h1 {
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    }

    .preview-hero h1 span {
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    .preview-lede {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
    }

    .access-note {
      max-width: 680px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      color: var(--dim);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.76rem;
    }

    .preview-section {
      padding: 5rem 2rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }


    .request-flow {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
      gap: 0.75rem;
      align-items: stretch;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .flow-card {
      min-width: 0;
      padding: 1.2rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: var(--surface2);
    }

    .featured-flow {
      border-color: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.4);
      background: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.055);
    }

    .flow-card > span,
    .card-label,
    .tier-kicker {
      display: block;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.68rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .flow-card strong,
    .flow-card small {
      display: block;
    }

    .flow-card strong {
      margin-top: 0.6rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .flow-card small {
      margin-top: 0.45rem;
      color: var(--dim);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .flow-arrow {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      color: var(--dim);
    }

    .preview-pillars,
    .included-grid,
    .tier-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
    }

    .preview-pillars,
    .included-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .preview-pillars {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .preview-pillars article {
      padding: 1.4rem;
      border: 1px solid rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.28);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.04);
    }

    .preview-pillars h3 {
      margin: 0.6rem 0 0.45rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .preview-pillars p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.86rem;
    }

    .included-grid article,
    .tier-card {
      padding: 1.4rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: var(--surface2);
    }

    .included-grid h3,
    .tier-card h3 {
      margin: 0.6rem 0 0.45rem;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .included-grid p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.86rem;
    }

    .tier-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .preview-tier {
      border-color: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.45);
      background: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.05);
    }

    .tier-card ul {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      margin: 1rem 0 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .tier-card li {
      position: relative;
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.86rem;
    }

    .tier-card li::before {
      content: "✓";
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      color: var(--accent);
    }

    .boundary-note {
      margin-top: 2rem;
      padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      background: rgba(0, 168, 173, 0.045);
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .boundary-note strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .access-container {
      max-width: 820px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .access-container p:not(.cta-meta) {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .request-flow,
      .included-grid,
      .tier-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .flow-arrow {
        justify-content: center;
        transform: rotate(90deg);
        min-height: 24px;
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .preview-hero {
        padding: 5rem 1rem 3.5rem;
      }

      .preview-section {
        padding: 3.5rem 1rem;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
